Taking into account that the phase transitions in L12-superstructures are discontinuous (occurrence of two phases with different compositions, one ordered and one not, in equilibrium with each other), in contrast to B2-phases, the virtual critical temperature Tc performs to a virtual transition temperature Tt, were one of the phase becomes unstable. These points were evaluated from the dependence of LRO as a function of temperature, from the point where the LRO parameter h goes to zero.

Four compounds, i.e., Ni3Al, Ni3Ga, Pt3Ga, and Pt3In, have been chosen for an application of the derived model equations to study the variation of thermodynamic activity and defect concentration. These intermetallic compounds crystallize in the ordered L12-structure with a pronounced tendency to LRO. The full sets of pair interaction energies suggested for these compounds are listed in the Table 1, accompanied by the hypothetical order–disorder transition temperatures at the stoichiometric composition and the corresponding disorder parameters at the given temperatures.

