\begin{title}
4. CONCLUSIONS
\end{title}

In summary, a combined theoretical and experimental investigation is carried out to study the He behavior in HEA TiZrHfMoNb and pure Ti. Formation energy calculations show that a He atom prefers to occupy the tetrahedral and octahedral interstitial sites in HEA and He clustering in HEA is more diﬃcult than that in pure Ti. The migration energy barrier for He in TiZrHfMoNb is calculated to be 0.27−0.96 eV compared with the value of 0.24 eV in Ti. The TEM analysis reveals that the sizes of He bubbles in a TiZrHfMoNb ﬁlm are generally smaller than those in Ti. Moreover, TiZrHfMoNb presents a weaker coarsening eﬀect relative to Ti. This study thus suggests that the TiZrHfMoNb HEA is more resistant to He bubble formation than Ti, which may have resulted from the suppressed He clustering, weaker coarsening eﬀect, and severe lattice distortion in HEA. The presented results may pave a way for designing new He damage tolerance structural materials for nuclear applications.

