Au

of the noble-metal nanoalloys that are induced by Cu-/Ni- assisted intermediates require high-temperature calcination treatment,8,9 which limits the preparation process of multi- component alloys. As a special material, mercury (Hg) can form amalgams with most conventional solid metals such as Au, Ag, and Pd.10 Despite the potential toxicity in the environment and biology, Hg exhibits unique and irreplaceable characteristics in nano-/microscale research, such as catalysis, battery materials, and environmental analysis.11 For example,

