Based on Figure 1, it is impossible to definitively determine the structure of individual agglomerates smaller than 5 nm. Thus, MD modeling in this case serves a predictive function, and at these scales, it predicts the surface segregation of Cu. At scales around 5 μm, considering the porosity of the obtained samples and based on the EDX element mapping, it is reasonable to conclude a highly homogeneous distribution of both Cu and Ni atoms.

